{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790462568,"nonce":"dto2yPl5BcdqlaIAsl4BgigJXfs=","title":"Side modules cannot load into a threaded wasm program","message":"A `wasm32-wasip1-threads` program imports a shared memory. A side module\nbuilt for `wasm32-wasip1` imports a plain one, so ash-wasm-run refuses it:\n\n    [ash] cannot load t2/hello.wasm: incompatible import type for `env::memory`\n\nBuilding the library for `wasm32-wasip1-threads` instead (pic,\n+mutable-globals, build-std, `rust-lld -flavor wasm -shared --shared-memory`)\nfails to link:\n\n    relocation R_WASM_MEMORY_ADDR_TLS_SLEB cannot be used against an\n    undefined symbol `errno`\n\nRust's std reaches errno as a thread-local, and a side module cannot\nTLS-relocate against an imported symbol. Reproducer: the hello library from\nwebsite/wasm.html (hl_abi + define_prim), built both ways.\n\nOptions: a no_std library over hl_abi (hl_abi itself uses std today), the\nprogram exporting a TLS offset for errno, or the loader giving each side\nmodule its own TLS block (`__tls_base` import) the way wasm-ld's dylink\nconvention expects. build_wasm_hdll.py builds wasip1 only.","files":null}]}